result:
The fix is commit `cd6cf1fc` (PR #1943, ticket O3-6093), "Improve support for arrow functions in expression variable extractor." It replaced the old `isLocalExpression` flag with a `boundNames` set. Arrow-function parameters go into that set and are inherited by nested arrows. `visitIdentifier` only reports a name if it is not a global and not in `boundNames`. Before the fix, the arrow visitor returned body variables through a return value that was dropped, so `f` and `b` in `a.map(x => f(b))` were lost.

**Implementation (esm-core, `packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts`)**
- `visitArrowFunctionExpression` collects the parameter names and visits the body with the extended `boundNames`: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:111-120}
- `visitIdentifier` adds a name only when it is not a global and not bound: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:150-154}
- `EvaluationContext` now carries `boundNames` in place of `isLocalExpression`: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:158-164}
- `createContextInternal` initialises `boundNames`: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:170-176}
- The public entry point `extractVariableNames`: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:47-56}

**Tests**
- Arrow-function cases, including `a.map(x => f(b))` expected to yield `['a', 'f', 'b']`: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.test.ts:46-63}

**Changeset**
- Patch note for `@openmrs/esm-expression-evaluator` and `@openmrs/esm-framework`: @file:{openmrs-esm-core::.changeset/flat-mammals-fail.md:1-7}

**Commits and PR**
- Fix commit `cd6cf1fc`, which I confirmed by diffing against its parent `9ea60732`. The diff removes the return-value propagation and the `isLocalExpression` flag.
- Earlier commit `9ea60732` (PR #1884), which introduced the `isLocalExpression` approach that the fix replaces.

I ran the diff for `extractor.ts` only. I did not run the test suite, so the test expectations are read from the file, not executed.

